      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "द्विपदण्ड &c. may be thus rendered : “Wicked destiny like",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "a potter places the mind like earth after perforce making a ball of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "it upon the wheel of care evermoving in consequence of its being",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "used to a series of strokes from a multitude of pole-like afflictions.”",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "विधिः खलः comp. Nîtis'ataka St. 94.—Hâriṇî.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. XCIX.—भेदप्रतिपत्ति = belief of difference. तयोः refers to महेश्वरे",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "and जनार्दने for which construction compare Gîtâ II., 4. The loca-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "tive is construed with भेद.—Vans'astha.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. C.—टङ्करव is scarcely susceptible of a good explanation.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "टंकारित is more common and better.—S'ârdûlavikrîdita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CI.—भैक्ष see St. 52 : अतिविमला मित्रामित्रसमानता comp. समः शत्रौ",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "च मित्रे च in Gîtâ XII., 18. The commentary takes अतिविमला चिन्ता",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "which is also good and perhaps supported by St. 90. ध्वस्ता ॰ ॰ ॰ ॰ प्र-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "मादास्तैर्मुदिताः commentary ; better ध्वस्ताः अशेषमदप्रमादाः येन सः and then",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "स चासौ मुदितश्च. The commentator joins the first three lines with",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "the last by अतः कारणात् (i. e. hence.) योगी नित्यमुक्तः संसारे सुखं तिष्ठति.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "Better perhaps, “With these.”—S'ârdûlavikrîdita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. CII.—तैरेव चायं भवः = and this world is constituted of them",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "only. In कस्येव, एव if taken अनवक्लृप्तौ (since the ordinary sense is not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "appropriate) would require कस्येव (Siddh. Kaum. I., 47)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "hence कस्येह must be held to be better. परिभ्रमत which it will be",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "seen is the reading of all except only two of the MSS. is the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "imperative. The construction is common as in किं स वत्सः करोतु in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "the Uttararâmacharita p. 127 and elsewhere. The translation",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "would be “ why should you wander” instead of “ why do you",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "wander” पाशशान्ति involves a clash of figures disapproved of in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "English Rhetoric but see Kâvyâdars'a p. 149 (II., 93). कामोच्छित्तिवशे",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "स्वधामनि = स्वकीये शरीरमन्दिरे कामोच्छित्तिवशे कन्दर्पजयार्थम् (commentary)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "विषयभोगत्यागेन अधीने स्वस्थानके हृदये एकाग्रतायामित्यर्थः (Râmarshi.) Rightly ;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "only स्वधामन् means आत्मतेजस्.—S'ârdûlavikrîdita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
